From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:58:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: free what a destroyed context's programs can no longer
 use

A gfx program is reachable only through the context that created it, but
its shaders hold its references, and the screen's live shader cache shares
one shader with every context that compiles the same source. Destroying a
context marks its programs removed and leaves them to their shaders. A
program with a shader another live context still uses then keeps every
pipeline it built, its shader variants, its pipeline cache, its library
set and the driver state behind them for as long as that shader lives,
although nothing can ever bind it again.

virglrenderer serves every guest GL client through one screen, and
Android's UI toolkit compiles the same shaders in every app, so each app a
guest started and closed left its pipelines behind for good: on
KosmicKrisp about 25-35 Metal render pipelines, their compute prologues
and the generated MSL per launch, without bound.

Track each gfx program on its context's list, under a screen lock, and
when the context is destroyed free the pipelines, pipeline cache, shader
variants and library reference of every program still on it. The program
itself still goes with its last shader.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c |  2 +
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.h |  3 +
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c  |  1 +
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h   |  8 +++
 5 files changed, 109 insertions(+)

